<h1 class="page-title">Sound Design</h1>
<p class="standfirst">Game audio: sound design, music and implementation.</p>

<p>I make the sounds for games, and the systems that make them react: foley and creature sounds, adaptive music, interfaces, and the Blueprints, scripts and FMOD events that tie it all to what the player is doing. Most of this work comes from my time at RMIT, working with game and animation teams.</p>

<h2>Projects</h2>
<dl class="index">
  <dt><a href="/sound-design/alchemeow/">Alchemeow</a></dt>
  <dd>Sound design lead and composer for a physics-based co-op game about two cats brewing potions, one paw each.</dd>
  <dt><a href="/sound-design/cyberpedia/">Cyberpedia</a></dt>
  <dd>Music and sound for a point-and-click museum adventure that sounds like a 90s CD-ROM.</dd>
  <dt><a href="/sound-design/okiro/">Okiro</a></dt>
  <dd>Sound, music and Unreal Engine implementation for a 3D puzzle adventure, out on Steam.</dd>
  <dt><a href="/sound-design/a-little-bit-of-gore/">A Little Bit of Gore</a></dt>
  <dd>Monsters you track by ear, an adaptive horror score and FMOD occlusion, for a first-person horror game.</dd>
  <dt><a href="/sound-design/hubworld/">Hubworld</a></dt>
  <dd>Sound design for an animated short about the last day of an old virtual world.</dd>
  <dt><a href="/sound-design/feedra/">Feedra Prototype</a></dt>
  <dd>A prototype soundboard for running live sound at tabletop games and stage shows.</dd>
</dl>

<h2>What I do</h2>
<ul class="points">
  <li>Sound design: recording, foley, editing, layering and processing</li>
  <li>Music for games: themes and adaptive, layered scores</li>
  <li>Implementation: FMOD Studio with Unity and Unreal Engine, Unreal Blueprints and Unity C# scripts</li>
  <li>Interactive systems: occlusion, footsteps that change with the surface, physics-driven impacts, dialogue babble, music that changes with the game</li>
</ul>

<h2>Tools</h2>
<p>Reaper &middot; Logic Pro &middot; FMOD Studio &middot; Unity (C#) &middot; Unreal Engine 4 and 5 (Blueprints) &middot; Adventure Creator &middot; Kontakt &middot; BFXR &middot; Git and SVN</p>
